# Line-ending policy: store LF in the repository, compare normalized.
#
# WHY: without these rules, tools/editors that save files with CRLF make git
# report every touched file as "modified" (phantom diffs with zero real
# content). With `text=auto`, git normalizes to LF when staging and compares
# normalized content, so `git status`/`git diff` only ever show real changes
# regardless of the line endings on disk.
#
# Do not remove: this file is what keeps the working tree honest.
* text=auto

# Windows script types must keep CRLF on checkout so they run correctly on
# Windows even when autocrlf is unset or the checkout happens on Linux.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
